#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167709} :activity/id #uuid "7d091858-0b78-564e-a2aa-e0d5c9a7bb0e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049052 :topic/id #uuid "d5eeaed9-a618-5662-a81f-c1e67aebd8d7" :topic/math-academy-id 3264} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167643 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166806 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166644 :question/id #uuid "f78d6af8-1a67-50e5-a1d0-6afbbe2b7c16" :question/math-academy-id "e-8452"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280d5568-b89a-5f92-97b1-a0489f139705" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050372}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167435} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167518} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538968} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538975} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539018} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563720} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563744}] :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square to Compute a Hyperbolic Arsecant Integral"} :step/id #uuid "99ea624f-69a6-5d1d-a35f-18894419a306" :step/math-academy-id 31484 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167645}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167644 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166807 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166645 :question/id #uuid "cde0faf2-8650-59c7-9a28-073516b09594" :question/math-academy-id "e-8453"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a67a245-b5be-5fe5-b6e4-c4a5f4bee054" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048610}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167433} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167434} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538926} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538953} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539016}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Integral Containing a Completed Square"} :step/id #uuid "0f6c3062-9d6c-592d-a31f-5fb2ead310cd" :step/math-academy-id 31485 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167643}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167645 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166808 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166646 :question/id #uuid "26cd55d1-dc94-507c-bcf9-13d619493184" :question/math-academy-id "e-8454"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f97720d6-2c67-5017-bf20-8045a8bb30b5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167436} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167519} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538970} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538980} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539028} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563668} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563699}] :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square to Compute a Hyperbolic Arcosecant Integral"} :step/id #uuid "60e05d0f-21d0-5754-8412-0060020c8e21" :step/math-academy-id 31486 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167646}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167646 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166809 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166647 :question/id #uuid "aa11660f-ce84-52df-bcc4-45a6d63b6d7e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8455"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6640d03e-5194-5a31-9315-007e59732446" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167437} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167438} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538982} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539017} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563651}] :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square to Compute a Hyperbolic Arcotangent Integral"} :step/id #uuid "754cf784-bf5d-5f7b-8c12-79b57d3e1f4b" :step/math-academy-id 31487} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167709 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168099 :tutorial/content "We can also complete the square to integrate hyperbolic *arcsecant*, *arccosecant*, and *arccotangent*.\n\nFor example, let's consider the integral\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)\\sqrt{-x^2-6x}} \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nAs it is, this integral doesn't resemble any of the basic integrals we have encountered so far. However, we can complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-6x & =-({x}^{2}+6x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =-((x+3)^{2}-9) \\\\  & =9-(x+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we plug the above into our integral and collect a factor of $9$ under the square root, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x+3)\\sqrt{9-(x+3)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{3(x+3)\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+3}{3})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis now looks more familiar! Let $u = \\dfrac {x+3}{3}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = 3\\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+3}{3})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a basic integral for an inverse reciprocal hyperbolic function, and we can solve it in one step:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "5f0c7466-a41d-5101-b125-8e6f68fba3ea" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5218 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "98b81a6a-5fdd-53d9-a014-da6921adf68b" :step/math-academy-id 32703 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167644}}] :activity/title "Integration Using Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions and Completing the Square" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167030}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046668} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563795} :activity/id #uuid "0cd59e01-3499-5e0d-9dff-47c2f8678675" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049052 :topic/id #uuid "d5eeaed9-a618-5662-a81f-c1e67aebd8d7" :topic/math-academy-id 3264} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563769 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563651 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09596fbb-5f17-590f-b8c6-41aea4206883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\frac{3x+2}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562958} {:answer/id #uuid "85052561-0afa-5d49-a8cd-46da05f90e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\frac{3x+2}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563244} {:answer/id #uuid "8adcb99e-b119-5618-808f-7b0725c00dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563254} {:answer/id #uuid "e08a4d2f-d017-5f6c-b6cc-e8a0f88c0fb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563438} {:answer/id #uuid "e861d624-48ec-543a-aaf6-deee37e2e5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\frac{3x+2}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563244} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fbff315-ecc9-5c1a-aaa6-d1781060ca7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1369cbfd-a46c-5064-baa1-cbe5720fb540" :question/math-academy-id "q-97910" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{16-(3x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{16-(3x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{16-16(\\frac{1}{16}(3x+2)^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\frac{3x+2}{4})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{3x+2}{4}|>1.$"} :step/id #uuid "227deb9f-a9be-5caf-9b21-75db4f696e28"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563781 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a472c55-b621-565c-b578-f92c20cbb266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563146} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7d1c78-ae26-55ef-86e8-9c531b3f1a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563193} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7b4cd4-4878-5393-9a31-5c5c09f3bcdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563367} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb986c7-c26a-5de1-8745-8a63847438c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563431} {:answer/id #uuid "fba7141a-d135-5744-8bbd-0158aa2f9308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563508}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563508} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b36eef3-f0c2-5b45-97f7-a2607c73a159" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "38a6fd7f-85a4-5b9d-9914-3bd5a2ab420c" :question/math-academy-id "q-97904" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|x-5|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+27}}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x+27 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2}+27 \\\\  & =(x-5)^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|x-5|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+27}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|x-5|\\sqrt{2+(x-5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{2+2{(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{|\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{|\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}})+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "49d1f9ce-7282-5ee1-8586-6e53e7242013" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563798}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563795 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb145f1-f9ae-5d5e-9acb-c2e8557eb522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562967} {:answer/id #uuid "259a3844-82ae-5b24-a85f-f38b2f21f870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563031} {:answer/id #uuid "4e03b87e-8d9e-547f-803e-f3b920ae8222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563122} {:answer/id #uuid "aa279346-be14-5108-9c91-ebb49fea3432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563328} {:answer/id #uuid "bb94fb36-58d4-5f5c-9e67-67e40c60505c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563328} :answer-field/id #uuid "0526b46b-564d-561d-a9aa-fedc41539160" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a95ee677-1642-5975-8b50-8432d56de160" :question/math-academy-id "q-97770" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x}}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-4x & =-({x}^{2}+4x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =-((x+2)^{2}-4) \\\\  & =4-(x+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{4-(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2(x+2)\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+2}{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+2}{2})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+2}{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x+2}{2}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+2}{2})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+2}{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9ddb5345-ef98-5ee3-a8a7-421a3b7a527f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563802}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563798 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563699 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a909a9b-174b-5639-8410-d7e274a5815f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563147} {:answer/id #uuid "6890919f-3dff-518f-b537-36ec02be3bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563186} {:answer/id #uuid "7f16f630-7db7-5f3c-9f65-39971597a4cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563223} {:answer/id #uuid "ba54fe97-ce78-59e0-ba7b-9401d786d8de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563353} {:answer/id #uuid "e66f808f-00b9-5dfa-be64-b5ad0a17a5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563353} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a55f92-f39f-5881-94c0-2f84b4c3471a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6a55ffae-eeb7-54cf-a5ce-c644ed8a6a5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97905" :question/problem "$\\int -\\frac{15}{|5x+10|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5}}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+5 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}+5 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int -\\frac{15}{|5x-10|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\int \\frac{15}{5|x+2|\\sqrt{1+(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-3\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{1+(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=x+2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-3\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{1+(x+2)^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =-3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡u+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "aaa68476-6aa2-5a3d-89b3-b111ae8473a4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563769}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563802 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1065a3b5-7eb0-5108-b4e2-8a64406d6063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562978} {:answer/id #uuid "39d34837-ebfe-5409-b1ab-da122aa01d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563075} {:answer/id #uuid "4c246a52-305e-5adb-972f-c828583b7f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563115} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8de859-a1f8-5dd2-834f-fa91b60b37c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563215} {:answer/id #uuid "b61c450a-f091-5a01-bd84-81b3a853a9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563347}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d9e3fb-7750-5a4b-a417-c4a5e9cfd326" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d6b27f7b-e94e-5d63-abcb-feb8d8bed4dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-97777" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-6x & =-({x}^{2}+6x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =-((x+3)^{2}-9) \\\\  & =9-(x+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{9-{(x+3)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+3}{3})\\sqrt{9-9{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+3}{3})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x+3}{3}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{(\\frac{x+3}{3})\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{x+3}{3})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b873437c-8a91-5a52-b7b4-61177581823b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563781}}] :activity/title "Integration Using Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions and Completing the Square" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562923}]}
